  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to authorizing the building inspector in the town of Wheatfield, county of Niagara, to reside outside such town",
    "basePrintNo": "S6182",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6182-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6182\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the town law and the public officers\nlaw, in relation to authorizing the building inspector in the town of\nWheatfield, county of Niagara, to reside outside such town\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 23 of the town law by adding a new\nsubdivision 28, providing that the person performing the functions of\nbuilding inspector in the town of Wheatfield, county of Niagara, need\nnot be an elector of such town.\n\nSection two amends section 3 of the public officers law by adding a\nnew subdivision 62, providing that the Person performing the functions\nof building inspector in the town of Wheatfield, county of Niagara,\nneed not be a resident of such town, provided that the person resides\nwithin the county of Niagara or an adjoining county within the state\nof New York.\n\nSection three is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would provide more flexibility for the town of\nWheatfield in hiring a building inspector.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
